<%# The way back from a page to the one it belongs to, at the top of the page, below any nav: Return to <to>. A page that
    also opens in a modal needs one (test_modal_pages_start_with_a_way_back), as whoever opens its URL has no modal to close %>
<a class="d-inline-block mb-3" href="<%= path %>"><i class="bi bi-arrow-left"></i> Return to <%= to %></a>
